WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.220
This is Centaur.

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:08.640
A brand new CRM solution with AI agents built in, that does the admin for your sales team,

3
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.700
so they can spend more time selling.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.840
Alex is a rep who starts the day already up to date.

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.920
Centaur lines up what needs his attention, with the most important tasks at the top of the list.

6
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.930
Meanwhile, the Centaur agents have been busy:

7
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.730
drafting replies to incoming emails, opening deals,

8
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.010
updating the deal records from intelligence picked up from Teams calls, notes and emails,

9
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.660
and preparing meeting briefs for the day ahead.

10
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.850
Here's one of them now.

11
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.400
Hannah, at Granite Learning Trust, sent an inquiry.

12
00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:49.070
She has a sales team of forty reps and currently using Pipedrive, asking about pricing.

13
00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:53.420
The agent replied, and asked some relevant qualification questions:

14
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:59.890
in this case, it's asked how many CRM users do you have, and when do you want to buy something by.

15
00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.750
Hannah answered the questions. Budget agreed,

16
00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.770
and they want a new system up and running before Christmas.

17
00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:11.960
So the agent offered a call with Cody, and sent an invite for a Teams call.

18
00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.090
Then, Centaur did all the admin.

19
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.820
It created the account, the contact and the deal,

20
00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:24.100
set the value from the email thread, and noted Pipedrive as the incumbent product.

21
00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:30.370
It qualified the deal against the chosen sales methodology: in this case, BANT.

22
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.850
And at this point, nobody has had to type a thing.

23
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:38.710
As things change, Centaur keeps the deal up to date, automatically.

24
00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.000
Before the call, Hannah writes again:

25
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.720
55 users now, signing by December 15th,

26
00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.350
and they're also looking at another product: HubSpot.

27
00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:56.060
The agent flags HubSpot as a risk, adds it as a competitor, and refreshes the deal summary.

28
00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.200
Then it suggests the new value and close date.

29
00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.130
One click each, and the deal is current.

30
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.680
Through all this automation, you still have the option to stay in full control.

31
00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:13.590
Every draft waits for your approval, until you're happy to let the agents send on their own.

32
00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.650
Centaur CRM.

33
00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.040
Give your sales team their time back.

34
00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.990
Book a demonstration today, at centaurcrm.com.
